%rec: default
# affixes.rec: the magic item affixes, one record each: a prefix goes before the item's name ("Fine Dagger"), a suffix
# after it ("Dagger of the Leech"). A magic item rolls at most one of each, among those whose min_level lies between
# half its item level and its item level, so an affix is only found in that band: give a power tiers.
# Fields:
#   internal_name     its id; required
#   name              as it reads in the item's name
#   slot              prefix or suffix
#   power             what it grants, a name savePower knows (src/rules/gen.go): to_hit, damage_percent, strength,
#                     light_radius, thorns, triple_damage, mana_on_kill, ...
#   values            the power's range "min-max", rolled between them (one number: fixed)
#   min_level         the item level it starts at
#   on                the items it may appear on: weapon bow staff armor shield jewelry
#   alignment         neutral (default), cursed or good; an item never carries a cursed prefix and a good suffix
#   double            true: it counts twice in the roll
#   in_good_rolls     false: it never rolls where only good powers are allowed (premium stock, quest rewards)
#   price             the item's added value at the low and the high end of values, "min-max"
#   price_multiplier  how strongly it multiplies the item's base value

